{"5224900":{"success":true,"data":{"type":"game","name":"Timberland","steam_appid":5224900,"required_age":0,"is_free":false,"dlc":[5271840],"detailed_description":"<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><u><i><strong>When night falls, your village had better be ready.<\/strong><\/i><\/u><\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You start with a handful of settlers in a voxel valley nobody has walked before. You don't place buildings and watch them appear: you assign trades. One fells trees, one cuts stone, one takes the carpenter's bench. What comes off their hands is what makes the next trade possible, until the valley becomes a village.<\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Trades that depend on each other<\/strong><\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Woodcutter, miner, stonecutter, carpenter, blacksmith, weaver, farmer, shepherd, forager, engineer, builder, soldier and archer. The log the woodcutter brings becomes planks at the carpenter's bench; those planks raise the workshop where the blacksmith smelts the ore the miner hauls up. Every trade levels up by working, and the better they get, the faster they work and the less they waste.<\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>A year you can feel<\/strong><\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Seasons here are more than a change of color. Vegetables sprout in spring, summer crops grow on their own, in autumn only what the farmer tends in person makes progress, and winter runs on what you stored. The days get shorter, and so do the working hours.<\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Eat, sleep, grow, survive<\/strong><\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Your settlers get hungry and tired. With no food they go out for berries; with no bed they collapse where they stand. And every spare bed is someone who will walk into town the next morning.<\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Night brings company<\/strong><\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >When the sun goes down, whatever lives past the fog comes out. Mark guard posts, set a soldier patrolling and an archer where it counts. Once a year something far worse arrives, and that one crosses the river along the bottom.<\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Your valley, your rules<\/strong><\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Every world grows from a seed, with its own terrain, river and forests. Pick a size and a difficulty, or open the generator sliders and decide how much stone, how many trees and how hungry you want to be.<\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >And more<\/h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Dig and build voxel by voxel, with cubes, slabs and ramps.<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Fog of war: what nobody has seen yet isn't on your map.<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A crafting queue for your workshops, to order things ahead.<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Objectives to point the way when you're not sure what's next.<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Drop down to ground level and see your village through a settler's eyes.<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Save and pick it up whenever you like.<\/p><\/li><\/ul>","about_the_game":"<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><u><i><strong>When night falls, your village had better be ready.<\/strong><\/i><\/u><\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You start with a handful of settlers in a voxel valley nobody has walked before. You don't place buildings and watch them appear: you assign trades. One fells trees, one cuts stone, one takes the carpenter's bench. What comes off their hands is what makes the next trade possible, until the valley becomes a village.<\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Trades that depend on each other<\/strong><\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Woodcutter, miner, stonecutter, carpenter, blacksmith, weaver, farmer, shepherd, forager, engineer, builder, soldier and archer. The log the woodcutter brings becomes planks at the carpenter's bench; those planks raise the workshop where the blacksmith smelts the ore the miner hauls up. Every trade levels up by working, and the better they get, the faster they work and the less they waste.<\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>A year you can feel<\/strong><\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Seasons here are more than a change of color. Vegetables sprout in spring, summer crops grow on their own, in autumn only what the farmer tends in person makes progress, and winter runs on what you stored. The days get shorter, and so do the working hours.<\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Eat, sleep, grow, survive<\/strong><\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Your settlers get hungry and tired. With no food they go out for berries; with no bed they collapse where they stand. And every spare bed is someone who will walk into town the next morning.<\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Night brings company<\/strong><\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >When the sun goes down, whatever lives past the fog comes out. Mark guard posts, set a soldier patrolling and an archer where it counts. Once a year something far worse arrives, and that one crosses the river along the bottom.<\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Your valley, your rules<\/strong><\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Every world grows from a seed, with its own terrain, river and forests. Pick a size and a difficulty, or open the generator sliders and decide how much stone, how many trees and how hungry you want to be.<\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >And more<\/h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Dig and build voxel by voxel, with cubes, slabs and ramps.<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Fog of war: what nobody has seen yet isn't on your map.<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A crafting queue for your workshops, to order things ahead.<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Objectives to point the way when you're not sure what's next.<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Drop down to ground level and see your village through a settler's eyes.<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Save and pick it up whenever you like.<\/p><\/li><\/ul>","short_description":"A voxel village, thirteen trades and a whole year ahead. Chain workshops together, sow with winter in mind and post a watch: when night falls, your village had better be ready.","supported_languages":"English, Spanish - Spain, French, Italian, German, Spanish - Latin America, Portuguese - Brazil, Portuguese - Portugal","header_image":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5224900\/6862ce377a6cf39df5bacdd6493257de838974db\/header.jpg?t=1793690540","capsule_image":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5224900\/09a76c9c2f435403de7fdad9ae677ee02e737381\/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1793690540","capsule_imagev5":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5224900\/09a76c9c2f435403de7fdad9ae677ee02e737381\/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1793690540","website":null,"pc_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operating system<br><\/li><li><strong>OS:<\/strong> Windows 10 64-bit<br><\/li><li><strong>Processor:<\/strong> Intel Core i3-8100 \/ AMD Ryzen 3 1200<br><\/li><li><strong>Memory:<\/strong> 4 GB RAM<br><\/li><li><strong>Graphics:<\/strong> DirectX 11 compatible with 1 GB VRAM (Intel UHD 620 \/ Radeon Vega 8)<br><\/li><li><strong>DirectX:<\/strong> Version 11<br><\/li><li><strong>Storage:<\/strong> 1 GB available space<\/li><\/ul>","recommended":"<strong>Recommended:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operating system<br><\/li><li><strong>OS:<\/strong> Windows 10\/11 64-bit<br><\/li><li><strong>Processor:<\/strong> Intel Core i5-10400 \/ AMD Ryzen 5 3600<br><\/li><li><strong>Memory:<\/strong> 8 GB RAM<br><\/li><li><strong>Graphics:<\/strong> NVIDIA GTX 1050 Ti \/ AMD RX 560 or better<br><\/li><li><strong>DirectX:<\/strong> Version 11<br><\/li><li><strong>Storage:<\/strong> 1 GB available space<\/li><\/ul>"},"mac_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>OS:<\/strong> macOS 12 Monterey<br><\/li><li><strong>Processor:<\/strong> Apple M1 \/ Intel Core i5 (2018)<br><\/li><li><strong>Memory:<\/strong> 4 GB RAM<br><\/li><li><strong>Graphics:<\/strong> Metal-compatible GPU (Apple M1 \/ Intel Iris Plus)<br><\/li><li><strong>Storage:<\/strong> 1 GB available space<\/li><\/ul>","recommended":"<strong>Recommended:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>OS:<\/strong> macOS 13 Ventura or later<br><\/li><li><strong>Processor:<\/strong> Apple M1 or better<br><\/li><li><strong>Memory:<\/strong> 8 GB RAM<br><\/li><li><strong>Graphics:<\/strong> Apple M1 GPU \/ AMD Radeon Pro 560X or better<br><\/li><li><strong>Storage:<\/strong> 1 GB available space<\/li><\/ul>"},"linux_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><\/ul>","recommended":"<strong>Recommended:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><\/ul>"},"developers":["LSM Games Studio"],"publishers":["LSM Games Studio"],"demos":[{"appid":5271840,"description":""}],"price_overview":{"currency":"USD","initial":999,"final":899,"discount_percent":10,"initial_formatted":"$9.99","final_formatted":"$8.99"},"packages":[1807490],"package_groups":[{"name":"default","title":"Buy Timberland","description":"","selection_text":"Select a purchase option","save_text":"","display_type":0,"is_recurring_subscription":"false","subs":[{"packageid":1807490,"percent_savings_text":"-10% ","percent_savings":0,"option_text":"Timberland - <span class=\"discount_original_price\">$9.99<\/span> $8.99","option_description":"","can_get_free_license":"0","is_free_license":false,"price_in_cents_with_discount":899}]}],"platforms":{"windows":true,"mac":true,"linux":false},"categories":[{"id":2,"description":"Single-player"},{"id":68,"description":"Custom Volume Controls"},{"id":78,"description":"Adjustable Difficulty"},{"id":79,"description":"Save Anytime"},{"id":23,"description":"Steam Cloud"},{"id":62,"description":"Family Sharing"}],"genres":[{"id":"4","description":"Casu